A||||6||Gokart||EGR probs may be solved!||||1||
Z||000000||Gokart||05-15-2000||09:01 PM||||Ponya and wxxo, found out today that there is supposed to be a "oriface" type gasket at the base of the tube where it meets the plenum. A member of egroups sent me instructions for replacing tube and it states: "IMPORTANT gasket with steel insert having small center hole MUST be installed at the inlet plenum end of the EGR valve adapter pipe assembly, with side identified as "tube side" towards pipe assembly." I know for sure I do not have this type gasket there. I will see if the Fiero Store will sell this gasket without buying tube tomorrow. <p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 05-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Linx||05-17-2000||02:16 AM||||At the plenum end?  Are you sure?  I thought it went on the <I>valve</I> end.  That gasket is a metal gasket- one of the lead looking ones...with a silver metal orifice in the center.  Because it was metal, I assumed it went on the hotter valve end of the hose.  And the gasket in my kit didnt fit the plenum end anyways.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||05-18-2000||05:43 AM||||The instructions I downloaded then printed came with a purchase of a new egr tube from the Fiero Store and they clearly say "the inlet plenum end of the egr valve adapter pipe assembly". If your not getting code 32 or egr probs I wouldn't worry about it. I posted this for those like me that are considering the electrical tape fix for that damn engine light <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000003||wxxo||05-18-2000||02:15 PM||||electric tape works for me. tired of foolin with that damn egr crap. you can chase it all day and just when you think that you have it the light goes on again. hate that damn light. hate it hate it hate it!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||jfuredy||05-19-2000||12:47 PM||||It may be easier to just tape over the light, but that will slow your car down.<P>When Code 32 is set the computer limits the amount of advance that your car can use, which limits its power.  After I fixed my EGR solenoid and reset the ECM there was a noticeable increase in performance.<P>Just something to think about.||||reg||1
Z||000005||wxxo||05-19-2000||01:50 PM||||help me out here. where is the solonoid? is it the thing with the diaphragm in it. or is it on the other side of the engine with the big hose in the back and the two smaller hoses coming out of the frount. (i got a v6 btw) i took that piece off and i can blow air through it. tasts like *&!@ and i dont recomend doing it yourself. but anyhow ive had that code 32 problem since i got the thing. the egr valve (diaphragm thing) is brand spankin new but that didnt solve the problem. what could it be??||||reg||1
